1
00:00:03,867 --> 00:00:10,900
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:37,767 --> 00:00:40,500
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:40,633 --> 00:00:42,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:45,267
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:54,167 --> 00:00:55,600
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:55,733 --> 00:00:58,133
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:58,267 --> 00:00:59,400
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:00:59,533 --> 00:01:01,000
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:02,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:06,100
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:08,633 --> 00:01:10,567
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:16,167
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:18,067
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:19,033 --> 00:01:20,767
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:21,467 --> 00:01:23,700
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:27,233
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:31,233 --> 00:01:33,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:34,867
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:36,367 --> 00:01:37,400
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:37,533 --> 00:01:39,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:43,833 --> 00:01:46,067
[BLOWS LANDING]

24
00:01:46,067 --> 00:01:47,400
<i>Want me to blow your head
into smithereens?</i>

25
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:48,900
<i>Do you know that I'm
an NCIA agent?!</i>

26
00:01:49,033 --> 00:01:50,367
<i>Our mission would have gone
smoothly.</i>

27
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:52,767
<i>But no! He still fought
with that man.</i>

28
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:54,700
<i>Who is that? Was he the one
who kissed you?</i>

29
00:01:54,833 --> 00:01:56,233
<i> One thing's for sure,</i>

30
00:01:56,367 --> 00:01:59,467
<i>I'd love to meet him
so I can finally catch him.</i>

31
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:03,367
<i>Sebastian was the one
who carried out the mission.</i>

32
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,633
<i> Sam just took the credit.</i>

33
00:02:05,767 --> 00:02:08,400
<i>And look for the man
who the group fought with.</i>

34
00:02:08,533 --> 00:02:10,967
<i>Because it's his fault
that I'm here right now.</i>

35
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:13,600
<i>I'll make sure he pays
for everything he did myself.</i>

36
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:14,767
<i> I'm from an NGO.</i>

37
00:02:14,933 --> 00:02:17,233
<i>I'm here to give Rudy's
financial aid</i>

38
00:02:17,367 --> 00:02:18,367
<i> to help his hospitalization.</i>

39
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,833
<i>You can't pay off
my father's hospitalization!</i>

40
00:02:19,967 --> 00:02:21,467
And I'll make sure, that whoever
<i> did that to my father,</i>

41
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,467
<i> will rot in jail! Leave!</i>

42
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,600
<i>Just because we're poor, we
can sell our dignity so easily?</i>

43
00:02:25,733 --> 00:02:27,867
<i>No! Whoever shot Father
will be imprisoned!</i>

44
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,800
<i>Even if it takes your father's
life in exchange?</i>

45
00:02:34,567 --> 00:02:36,900
[NEIL] How did it go, ma'am?

46
00:02:37,033 --> 00:02:38,233
They were
stubbornly against it.

47
00:02:38,367 --> 00:02:40,567
Especially the son.
He was too tough.

48
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:42,600
He's got an attitude.

49
00:02:46,167 --> 00:02:47,167
Ma'am! Ma'am!

50
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:48,900
[BETCHAY] Ma'am! Uh-oh!

51
00:02:49,067 --> 00:02:50,133
- Ma'am!
- Oh!

52
00:02:50,267 --> 00:02:52,333
- I'm here!
- Oh, Ma'am! [GIGGLING]

53
00:02:52,467 --> 00:02:54,533
Ma'am! [LAUGHS] Oh, Ma'am.

54
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:56,600
- Ma'am, I apologize.
- Yes, Miss.

55
00:02:56,733 --> 00:03:00,033
I'd like to apologize
on behalf of them.

56
00:03:00,167 --> 00:03:02,900
You were kind enough to help
but you were treated so harshly.

57
00:03:03,033 --> 00:03:05,267
Those two are way too stubborn

58
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,967
as opposed to me
who's easy to talk to!

59
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:10,033
Oh, ma'am, thank you so much
for understanding.

60
00:03:10,167 --> 00:03:12,667
I just really-- we just really
wanted to help out.

61
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:15,100
That's why I felt so bad
for you!

62
00:03:15,233 --> 00:03:16,900
Those two don't know
a single thing!

63
00:03:17,033 --> 00:03:19,967
They don't know how expensive
it is to be hospitalized!

64
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:23,833
The bill just gets bigger
as the days go by!

65
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,100
My god!

66
00:03:25,233 --> 00:03:27,833
We really can't afford it.

67
00:03:27,967 --> 00:03:30,533
Don't worry, ma'am. It will all
get better soon enough.

68
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:32,800
- I really hope so.
- Well, then!

69
00:03:33,467 --> 00:03:35,133
I hope this could help you.

70
00:03:35,267 --> 00:03:36,600
That's right. [LAUGHING]

71
00:03:36,733 --> 00:03:39,567
I'm so sorry this is all
we could give you

72
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:41,200
from our NGO.

73
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:45,200
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:03:45,333 --> 00:03:49,533
Uh... the antibiotic that Rudy
needs is expensive...

75
00:03:49,667 --> 00:03:51,867
this might not be enough
to buy it...

76
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,200
- Oh...
- [BETCHAY SIGHS]

77
00:03:54,367 --> 00:03:55,900
- for an antibiotic, huh.
- Mm-hmm...

78
00:03:56,533 --> 00:04:00,100
Alright, here. For Sir Rudy's
antibiotic. Here's some more.

79
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:04,367
- [BETCHAY BREATHES DEEPLY]
- [QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

80
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,567
Thank you so much! [CRYING]

81
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,700
This is a huge help
for us, truly!

82
00:04:08,833 --> 00:04:10,467
Oh, it's nothing. [LAUGHING]

83
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:12,467
Could I trouble you some more?

84
00:04:12,833 --> 00:04:15,600
Because we couldn't eat
anything at the hospital.

85
00:04:15,733 --> 00:04:17,067
The food is too expensive.

86
00:04:17,067 --> 00:04:19,700
We only drink water
and have soup.

87
00:04:19,833 --> 00:04:21,133
Oh, that's no trouble at all.

88
00:04:21,267 --> 00:04:23,967
Here for some delicious food
and drinks!

89
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:26,100
I believe that's more than
enough, isn't it?

90
00:04:26,233 --> 00:04:28,200
Oh, most definitely! Thank you
so much!

91
00:04:28,367 --> 00:04:31,733
You are the angel of my life!
Heaven-sent!

92
00:04:31,867 --> 00:04:34,200
- May God bless you!
- [LAUGHING]

93
00:04:34,333 --> 00:04:36,200
Oh, can we take
a photo together?

94
00:04:36,333 --> 00:04:38,267
- Oh, sure!
- For documentation purposes.

95
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:39,500
Sure! You don't have
to explain.

96
00:04:39,633 --> 00:04:40,933
[MAX LAUGHING LIGHTLY] Okay.

97
00:04:41,067 --> 00:04:42,833
- Is the lighting okay?
- [MAX CLEARS THROAT]

98
00:04:42,967 --> 00:04:44,067
- Am I in frame?
- Yeah.

99
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,833
- There. One, two, three.
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

100
00:04:46,967 --> 00:04:50,267
- One, two, three.
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

101
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,333
[DELGADO] Ah.

102
00:04:51,767 --> 00:04:52,667
Castor.

103
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:53,900
Is everyone here?

104
00:04:54,033 --> 00:04:54,867
Yes, sir!

105
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,533
Guys, sir wants to talk to us.

106
00:04:58,333 --> 00:04:59,567
Uh...

107
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:04,767
I have Chief Pia Catacutan's
review

108
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:08,367
on your successful mission.

109
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:09,533
Congratulations!

110
00:05:09,667 --> 00:05:11,167
- Thank you, sir!
- [DELGADO LAUGHING]

111
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:15,733
And most especially,
I would like to congratulate

112
00:05:16,033 --> 00:05:18,767
Special Agent Sebastian Tuazon.

113
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:23,367
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,267
Me? Wh-- why me?

115
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:28,667
Yes, you. Were you surprised
by the efforts you've done?

116
00:05:30,233 --> 00:05:34,400
Here is Chief Pia's review.

117
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:36,267
I'll read it to you.

118
00:05:36,533 --> 00:05:40,800
"Maintained strict adherence
to operation's directives

119
00:05:40,933 --> 00:05:42,300
and rules of engagement.

120
00:05:42,433 --> 00:05:45,367
Number two, demonstrated
exceptional

121
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,500
situational awareness

122
00:05:47,567 --> 00:05:49,833
under rapidly changing
conditions.

123
00:05:49,967 --> 00:05:51,067
And number three,

124
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:55,133
provided accurate
and timely intelligence updates

125
00:05:55,267 --> 00:06:00,533
that contributed significantly
to the success of the mission."

126
00:06:00,667 --> 00:06:07,200
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

127
00:06:07,367 --> 00:06:08,300
Well,

128
00:06:08,667 --> 00:06:11,267
thank you very much,
ma'am, sir.

129
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,700
I believe...

130
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:15,867
I just did what I had to do.

131
00:06:16,533 --> 00:06:19,467
Team, I'll give you, uh...

132
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,167
a copy of this report.

133
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:23,667
Sam,

134
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:25,867
to my office, please.

135
00:06:35,767 --> 00:06:37,267
[SEBASTIAN] Oh, thank you!

136
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,967
- Congratulations, sir.
- Thank you.

137
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:41,767
- Congratulations, sir.
- Thank you.

138
00:06:41,933 --> 00:06:44,667
- Congratulations, sir.
- Thank you so much.

139
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,533
Bro, will you
not congratulate me?

140
00:06:46,667 --> 00:06:48,400
Ah... congrats, bro.

141
00:06:48,733 --> 00:06:50,000
Thank you, thank you.

142
00:06:50,933 --> 00:06:51,900
Take a seat.

143
00:06:52,033 --> 00:06:57,300
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

144
00:06:57,433 --> 00:06:58,300
[THUDS]

145
00:06:58,667 --> 00:07:01,233
That's Ma'am Pia's report.

146
00:07:05,367 --> 00:07:08,167
Team Leader Jacinto
engaged in direct intervention

147
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:10,300
that unnecessarily increased...

148
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,933
operational risk to personnel?

149
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:16,100
Recommendation.
Formal written reprimand.

150
00:07:16,267 --> 00:07:19,600
Mandatory leadership and
operational compliance training.

151
00:07:19,733 --> 00:07:20,967
Possible suspension.

152
00:07:21,867 --> 00:07:25,000
Sir, this report has no basis.

153
00:07:25,133 --> 00:07:26,567
This report seems so biased.

154
00:07:26,567 --> 00:07:29,833
We need to respect that report.

155
00:07:30,267 --> 00:07:33,867
That is, evidence-based...
objective.

156
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,967
If that man wasn't involved
in your operation

157
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:39,667
the report would be different.

158
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:42,000
Sir, I know I am not perfect.

159
00:07:42,133 --> 00:07:44,567
I know I have a lot of things
to improve.

160
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:46,733
But I will fight
for what I did right

161
00:07:46,867 --> 00:07:48,267
during our mission
in Chinatown.

162
00:07:48,433 --> 00:07:50,300
Sam, you should focus on

163
00:07:51,367 --> 00:07:53,967
reviewing the rules
of engagement

164
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:59,267
and you'll undergo leadership
and compliance re-training!

165
00:07:59,733 --> 00:08:01,800
What about
my possible suspension?

166
00:08:01,933 --> 00:08:06,267
Sam, we need
to follow the process.

167
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:10,567
Whatever the board
sees as necessary,

168
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,400
that's what will happen.

169
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:16,167
[ELTON] Gabo!

170
00:08:17,167 --> 00:08:18,100
Gabo!

171
00:08:19,167 --> 00:08:20,867
Where did you take
the motorcycle?

172
00:08:22,233 --> 00:08:25,167
Elton, I used it for work.

173
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:28,900
There was a mishap,
so I had to leave it.

174
00:08:29,433 --> 00:08:31,267
- [CHAIR THUDS]
- You have no shame, Gabo!

175
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:33,600
Why would you do that?
Don't you know

176
00:08:33,667 --> 00:08:36,867
that the marine who owns it
will claim it today!

177
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:42,133
And the money he'll pay is
for your dad's medical expenses!

178
00:08:42,267 --> 00:08:43,433
- You're not thinking!
- [CLATTERS]

179
00:08:43,567 --> 00:08:46,533
Hey, Elton! Don't do that!

180
00:08:46,667 --> 00:08:49,500
Didn't he say
that he'd return it?

181
00:08:49,633 --> 00:08:50,800
Right, Gabo?

182
00:08:53,633 --> 00:08:54,633
Elton...

183
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:57,367
Please don't get mad.
I promise...

184
00:08:57,900 --> 00:08:59,567
I'll return
the motorcycle tomorrow.

185
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:02,333
I thought you've changed!

186
00:09:02,467 --> 00:09:03,867
Betchay was right!

187
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:11,000
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

188
00:09:11,933 --> 00:09:12,800
Hey.

189
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:15,100
Where's my motorcycle?

190
00:09:16,533 --> 00:09:18,300
- Well...
- Where's Rudy?

191
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:20,433
He's at the hospital.
He got shot.

192
00:09:20,567 --> 00:09:22,367
Who can I talk to about this?

193
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:25,467
- Where's Elton?
- He's at Rudy's house.

194
00:09:28,033 --> 00:09:29,233
[BRANDO] Is anyone home?

195
00:09:30,567 --> 00:09:32,100
- Is anyone home?
- Who's there?

196
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:34,567
[ELTON] Oh, Brando.

197
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,267
Elton, I'm here
to take the motorcycle.

198
00:09:37,367 --> 00:09:38,700
[ELTON] The motorcycle?

199
00:09:38,833 --> 00:09:41,667
There's a bit of a problem.

200
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:46,133
I took it to another mechanic,
but they're fixing it.

201
00:09:46,267 --> 00:09:48,733
I left it with you for six
months, and it's still broken?!

202
00:09:48,867 --> 00:09:50,433
When you gave it to me,

203
00:09:50,567 --> 00:09:52,233
the engine
was almost falling apart.

204
00:09:52,367 --> 00:09:54,933
We really tried fixing it!

205
00:09:55,067 --> 00:09:57,167
[BRANDO] And you have
the nerve to lie?

206
00:09:57,167 --> 00:09:58,833
I think you're all
just messing with me here!

207
00:09:59,567 --> 00:10:01,167
Sir, I'm sorry.

208
00:10:01,333 --> 00:10:02,800
Don't worry.

209
00:10:02,933 --> 00:10:05,600
I promise you'll get it
by tomorrow.

210
00:10:05,733 --> 00:10:06,700
Fine.

211
00:10:06,833 --> 00:10:09,567
Next time, we'll see
each other at the station.

212
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:13,100
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

213
00:10:13,233 --> 00:10:14,333
[SCREEM DOOR CLATTERS]

214
00:10:16,667 --> 00:10:17,867
Sir Brando!

215
00:10:18,567 --> 00:10:21,300
How are you?
Will you get your motorcycle?

216
00:10:21,433 --> 00:10:24,133
I was about to, but Elton
said it wasn't ready.

217
00:10:24,267 --> 00:10:27,167
Untll now, it's still broken!

218
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:29,033
I think they're just conning me.

219
00:10:29,167 --> 00:10:31,000
Those idiots.

220
00:10:31,133 --> 00:10:33,967
Let me talk to them.

221
00:10:34,567 --> 00:10:38,233
Could we ask for help
with Rudy's medical expenses?

222
00:10:38,367 --> 00:10:40,133
He was shot.

223
00:10:40,267 --> 00:10:41,800
He's still at the hospital

224
00:10:47,467 --> 00:10:50,500
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:10:50,633 --> 00:10:51,833
Thank you.

226
00:10:51,967 --> 00:10:56,433
But this won't even pay
for his antibiotics.

227
00:10:56,567 --> 00:10:58,667
- That's not enough, Betchay?
- Yes.

228
00:10:58,667 --> 00:11:01,267
He takes those for seven days.

229
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:03,333
Here. I think that's enough.

230
00:11:03,467 --> 00:11:05,633
It is enough, but...

231
00:11:05,767 --> 00:11:09,700
I haven't been able
to work since Rudy got shot.

232
00:11:09,867 --> 00:11:11,467
We can't afford anything to eat.

233
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:14,367
When we're at the hospital,
we just drink water.

234
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:17,200
Just to get by.

235
00:11:17,333 --> 00:11:19,333
What do I have to do with it?!

236
00:11:19,467 --> 00:11:21,867
The Lord will bless you.

237
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,133
Just take care
of my motorcycle, alright?

238
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:28,333
Don't worry.
They're all scared of me!

239
00:11:28,467 --> 00:11:31,033
I'll handle it.
Elton!

240
00:11:31,167 --> 00:11:33,900
Gabo, make sure
you take care of this.

241
00:11:34,033 --> 00:11:36,433
If you don't, then
I'll get dragged into this.

242
00:11:36,867 --> 00:11:39,967
[SCREEN DOOR CREAKS, SLAMS]

243
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:42,833
Badong, where's Elton?

244
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,233
He's inside.

245
00:11:44,833 --> 00:11:47,267
Hey, I saw Sir Brando.

246
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:49,367
Why isn't his motorcycle fixed?

247
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,500
It's already taking so long!

248
00:11:51,633 --> 00:11:54,133
Save it, Betchay.

249
00:11:54,267 --> 00:11:56,733
If there's one person
who you should ask about it,

250
00:11:56,867 --> 00:11:58,800
It's Gabo!

251
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:04,267
[SCREEN DOOR CREAKS, SLAMS]

252
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:05,867
What have you done?

253
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:08,000
What did you do
to the motorcycle?

254
00:12:08,133 --> 00:12:12,300
Gabo used it for work.

255
00:12:12,433 --> 00:12:15,500
Where did you leave it, Gabo?

256
00:12:17,867 --> 00:12:19,233
In Binondo.

257
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:22,233
But I'll get it back today.

258
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:28,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

259
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:30,733
You lied.

260
00:12:31,233 --> 00:12:33,400
You lied to Sir Brando.

261
00:12:34,033 --> 00:12:37,967
That's why he can't get it...

262
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:40,400
it's because you took it!

263
00:12:40,533 --> 00:12:42,067
You used it!

264
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:44,367
You showed off again!

265
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:46,033
You failed!

266
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:49,167
He was about to pay for it!

267
00:12:49,333 --> 00:12:53,767
We could've used that money
for your father's operation!

268
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:57,267
- Now that money's gone!
- That's enough!

269
00:12:57,400 --> 00:13:01,067
Didn't you hear?!
He said he'll return it!

270
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,467
What else do you want?!

271
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:09,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

272
00:13:09,167 --> 00:13:12,600
[CHAIR CLATTERS]

273
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:14,433
Don't worry.

274
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:16,767
I'll get it back.

275
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,333
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

276
00:13:28,333 --> 00:13:30,100
- [DOOR CLOSES]
- [PIA] Jacinto!

277
00:13:44,533 --> 00:13:46,733
I hope you're satisfied
with my report.

278
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,367
After all,

279
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,267
who wouldn't be happy
to see the truth come out?

280
00:13:53,567 --> 00:13:55,333
You're careless
on getting the job done.

281
00:13:55,367 --> 00:14:01,500
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

282
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,800
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

283
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:08,067
Have you guys
told Bullet your orders?

284
00:14:08,067 --> 00:14:09,333
- Yes, sir.
- Thank you.

285
00:14:09,333 --> 00:14:10,833
Sir Seb, thanks again.

286
00:14:10,833 --> 00:14:12,333
I hope the higher-ups are
always happy with your work.

287
00:14:12,333 --> 00:14:15,333
Oh, you're welcome.
It's nothing.

288
00:14:15,333 --> 00:14:18,333
We all know how great
the whole team was.

289
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,433
Oh, Sam, Sir Seb
will treat us all to coffee.

290
00:14:21,633 --> 00:14:23,600
I already told them
what you want. Cafe mocha.

291
00:14:24,933 --> 00:14:27,233
Ma'am Sam, aren't you going
to treat us to dinner later?

292
00:14:27,433 --> 00:14:28,733
You know, for the team.

293
00:14:28,767 --> 00:14:30,300
Come on, Ma'am Sam.
Treat us to dinner.

294
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:32,400
What did Sir Delgado say?

295
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,933
Are you getting promoted?

296
00:14:33,933 --> 00:14:35,133
That's for sure.

297
00:14:35,133 --> 00:14:36,333
She's totally getting promoted.

298
00:14:36,867 --> 00:14:39,433
Ma'am, does that mean
we're going to the buffet later?

299
00:14:39,433 --> 00:14:41,433
- [CHEERING, CLAPPING]
- We'll eat so much!

300
00:14:41,433 --> 00:14:42,867
Where to? Where to?

301
00:14:43,167 --> 00:14:44,133
No, we're not.

302
00:14:45,333 --> 00:14:46,433
I failed.

303
00:14:46,633 --> 00:14:48,433
What? What do you mean?

304
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:50,500
We caught Tiger.

305
00:14:51,767 --> 00:14:52,833
I don't know.

306
00:14:53,067 --> 00:14:54,500
They said I had many violations.

307
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:56,467
And they don't think
I'm a good leader.

308
00:14:57,167 --> 00:14:58,300
I might even be suspended.

309
00:14:58,500 --> 00:14:59,867
- Suspended?
- Suspended?

310
00:14:59,867 --> 00:15:00,967
- What?
- Why would you--

311
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:01,967
Why would they suspend you?

312
00:15:01,967 --> 00:15:03,200
- How so?
- What did you do?

313
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,267
Congratulations, coffee is here!

314
00:15:05,467 --> 00:15:07,433
For the best of the NCIA agents.

315
00:15:07,633 --> 00:15:11,700
Yes! Congratulations,
Sir Sebastian and Ma'am Sam.

316
00:15:11,933 --> 00:15:13,133
We did a great job.

317
00:15:14,533 --> 00:15:18,500
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

318
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:19,633
Cheer up!

319
00:15:19,633 --> 00:15:20,667
Why the long faces?

320
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:23,100
This is not the time
to celebrate!

321
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,733
It's okay.

322
00:15:27,067 --> 00:15:28,567
Come on, celebrate your win.

323
00:15:28,567 --> 00:15:30,967
You deserve it.
You did a job well done.

324
00:15:30,967 --> 00:15:32,233
No, no, no.

325
00:15:32,533 --> 00:15:34,267
We can't.
No one is going to celebrate.

326
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,467
Especially when there's
a threat of suspension.

327
00:15:36,767 --> 00:15:38,167
Threat of suspension?

328
00:15:38,167 --> 00:15:39,267
- Shh!
- Bullet!

329
00:15:40,167 --> 00:15:41,233
Keep it down, man.

330
00:15:42,267 --> 00:15:43,967
I don't know.
I just can't really accept it.

331
00:15:44,167 --> 00:15:47,200
I can't understand why
Ma'am Pia seems to dislike me.

332
00:15:47,467 --> 00:15:49,100
Like, I can't get
anything right,

333
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:50,533
and everything I do is wrong.

334
00:15:50,533 --> 00:15:54,167
Ma'am, I think Ma'am Pia
just has high standards.

335
00:15:54,167 --> 00:15:55,467
Really, Ernesto?

336
00:15:55,467 --> 00:15:58,700
Do you mean to say she can't do
the job up to her standards?

337
00:15:58,900 --> 00:16:00,667
Hold on, first of all,
Ma'am Sam is great.

338
00:16:00,667 --> 00:16:02,567
She gets the job done
anywhere on the field.

339
00:16:02,767 --> 00:16:04,600
Investigation--
One of the best.

340
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:06,867
I wasn't talking
about her skills.

341
00:16:06,867 --> 00:16:08,167
What I meant was...

342
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,700
my skills.

343
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:12,600
That's enough.
There's nothing we can do

344
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,733
but accept it.

345
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:18,500
Come on,
get back to your stations.

346
00:16:19,467 --> 00:16:20,533
Let me get mine.

347
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:23,100
I can't afford to pay the bills.

348
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:24,333
- Shh!
- And now this...

349
00:16:24,333 --> 00:16:26,467
- What?!
- Who is this about this time?

350
00:16:26,467 --> 00:16:27,667
Who else would it be?

351
00:16:27,667 --> 00:16:29,400
What has your nephew done again?

352
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:32,700
- Oh, please, give Gabo a break!
- Give him a break?!

353
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,567
We're talking about money!

354
00:16:34,567 --> 00:16:36,700
That can help pay
for the surgery! Now what?

355
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:38,000
He fooled around again.

356
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,433
And you always take his side!

357
00:16:39,867 --> 00:16:42,333
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

358
00:16:42,367 --> 00:16:43,333
Is he still here?

359
00:16:43,333 --> 00:16:44,700
- You're always like this.
- Stop it!

360
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:45,667
Every freaking day--

361
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:47,100
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

362
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:48,600
Gabo, where are you going?

363
00:16:50,867 --> 00:16:52,633
Hey, what's with the face?

364
00:16:53,333 --> 00:16:54,467
I have a problem.

365
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:57,000
I left the motorcycle
Papa was repairing.

366
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,967
I left it
where I should've caught Tiger.

367
00:16:59,933 --> 00:17:01,300
I need to get it back.

368
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:04,400
Don't go back there.
Someone might recognize you.

369
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:05,967
You might get
in trouble there, Gabo.

370
00:17:05,967 --> 00:17:07,067
I can't just abandon it.

371
00:17:08,433 --> 00:17:11,200
It's the only way
we could earn money.

372
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,500
We need it
to pay for Papa's surgery.

373
00:17:12,967 --> 00:17:14,333
We'll come with you, Gabo.

374
00:17:14,333 --> 00:17:15,500
- Mm-hmm.
- He's right.

375
00:17:15,733 --> 00:17:16,833
You might need some backup.

376
00:17:17,367 --> 00:17:18,333
We're here to help.

377
00:17:18,633 --> 00:17:19,633
Come on.

378
00:17:19,933 --> 00:17:20,933
Come on.

379
00:17:20,933 --> 00:17:22,200
[MUSIC FADES]

380
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,267
Sir, ma'am.

381
00:17:23,933 --> 00:17:25,333
I have spoken to Attorney.

382
00:17:25,767 --> 00:17:26,967
He came to visit Victor.

383
00:17:27,867 --> 00:17:29,133
Any updates?

384
00:17:29,133 --> 00:17:30,267
He's studying the case.

385
00:17:30,267 --> 00:17:32,500
He's finding ways
to get him out of there.

386
00:17:32,933 --> 00:17:35,167
Fortunately,
they didn't catch Mr. Chan.

387
00:17:35,167 --> 00:17:36,167
If he were,

388
00:17:36,733 --> 00:17:38,333
they'd have a stronger case
against Victor.

389
00:17:38,733 --> 00:17:42,900
Make sure Mr. Chan
keeps his mouth shut.

390
00:17:43,433 --> 00:17:44,400
Ma.

391
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,100
Let me handle it.

392
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:48,733
I'll make sure
he keeps his mouth shut.

393
00:17:49,767 --> 00:17:50,700
Sir.

394
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:52,567
There's something
Victor wants to tell you.

395
00:17:52,567 --> 00:17:54,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

396
00:17:54,133 --> 00:17:55,267
What is it?

397
00:17:55,267 --> 00:17:58,233
He was caught by the cops
because a man tackled him.

398
00:17:58,433 --> 00:17:59,333
Who is it?

399
00:17:59,533 --> 00:18:00,633
Is it someone from NCIA?

400
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:02,133
Give me the name.

401
00:18:02,333 --> 00:18:03,767
He's not from NCIA.

402
00:18:03,767 --> 00:18:05,067
Seems like he's a civilian.

403
00:18:05,533 --> 00:18:08,467
Sir, he wants us
to find that man.

404
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:09,967
He wants to get back at him.

405
00:18:11,067 --> 00:18:12,267
Who could that man be?

406
00:18:13,533 --> 00:18:15,933
Why is he messing
with our business?

407
00:18:15,933 --> 00:18:17,733
Is someone going against us?

408
00:18:18,067 --> 00:18:19,767
And are they targeting Victor?

409
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:21,467
Did you see the man?

410
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:23,367
Do you remember
what he looks like?

411
00:18:23,367 --> 00:18:24,400
No, Ma.

412
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,733
But I think there's a traitor
in our group.

413
00:18:27,367 --> 00:18:28,967
And that's what
got Victor in trouble.

414
00:18:29,433 --> 00:18:31,667
Find out who that animal is.

415
00:18:31,667 --> 00:18:32,667
Find him!

416
00:18:32,667 --> 00:18:34,100
And bring him to me.

417
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:36,433
I'll make him pay
for what he did to Victor.

418
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,300
Yes, sir, ma'am.

419
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:47,300
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

420
00:18:50,167 --> 00:18:55,733
Sam, don't you ever think
for a second you're not good.

421
00:18:57,067 --> 00:19:00,400
The whole team knows
how great you did.

422
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:03,867
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

423
00:19:03,867 --> 00:19:06,467
Why don't we
hang out later?

424
00:19:06,467 --> 00:19:09,400
- That sounds good!
- Wanna grab a drink? I'm down!

425
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:12,733
You know what, let's go out.
Let's get dinner.

426
00:19:12,733 --> 00:19:16,567
I know a new French place in
Makati. I'll make a reservation.

427
00:19:16,567 --> 00:19:18,667
That's a great idea, Sir Seb.

428
00:19:18,667 --> 00:19:19,933
Let's double date.

429
00:19:19,933 --> 00:19:22,767
You and Ma'am Sam at one table,
Karen and me at the other.

430
00:19:22,767 --> 00:19:24,233
What double date
are you talking about?

431
00:19:24,233 --> 00:19:25,300
It's just them.
Stay out of this.

432
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:28,833
- Who knows, maybe--
- Sam, what do you say?

433
00:19:28,867 --> 00:19:32,367
Maybe it's better
if it's just you and me.

434
00:19:32,367 --> 00:19:35,733
- What?
- Let's go on a date. Just us.

435
00:19:35,733 --> 00:19:37,533
You really don't quit, do you?

436
00:19:37,533 --> 00:19:42,467
Are you clueless,
or just trying to annoy me?

437
00:19:42,467 --> 00:19:43,700
No thanks.

438
00:19:45,433 --> 00:19:47,733
Come on, Sam.
I'm just trying to comfort you.

439
00:19:48,867 --> 00:19:51,833
Comfort?
I don't need to be comforted.

440
00:19:51,833 --> 00:19:55,100
You know what I need
with everything going on?

441
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:56,667
No more stress.

442
00:19:56,667 --> 00:20:01,067
And right now, that is exactly
what you are giving me.

443
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:05,067
[MUFFLED VOICE]
Well, someone's got attitude.

444
00:20:05,067 --> 00:20:09,133
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

445
00:20:09,133 --> 00:20:11,700
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

446
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,133
Sam...

447
00:20:15,133 --> 00:20:18,733
That was a bit too much.
You hurt his feelings.

448
00:20:18,733 --> 00:20:21,400
Please. I was actually
holding back.

449
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:24,967
Sam, don't you stress eat
when you're stressed?

450
00:20:24,967 --> 00:20:28,433
What a waste of a date.
It was French cuisine.

451
00:20:28,433 --> 00:20:31,033
What do you even see
in Sebastian anyway?

452
00:20:31,033 --> 00:20:35,567
You never stop trying
to play matchmaker.

453
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,733
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

454
00:20:36,733 --> 00:20:39,233
- You two are perfect together.
- No, we're not.

455
00:20:39,233 --> 00:20:42,933
Well, that's just your opinion.
And you're not always right.

456
00:20:42,933 --> 00:20:46,100
Let me ask you,
what don't you see in him?

457
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:49,233
He's perfect.
What are you looking for?

458
00:20:50,933 --> 00:20:54,333
Nothing, because I'm not
looking for a boyfriend.

459
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:58,067
But if the time comes
that I do meet someone,

460
00:20:58,067 --> 00:21:03,733
even if he takes me to
a cheap street food cart,

461
00:21:03,733 --> 00:21:07,867
as long as he makes me happy
and isn't annoying, I'd go.

462
00:21:07,867 --> 00:21:10,767
- You mean you'd date him?
- Yes.

463
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:14,200
A date, hanging out, food run,
whatever you want to call it.

464
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:18,600
If I'm happy with him
I'm good.

465
00:21:19,533 --> 00:21:20,900
Mm. Whatever.

466
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:27,200
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

467
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:30,900
- That's where I left my bike.
- Huh?

468
00:21:30,900 --> 00:21:34,667
Man, Gabo.
The whole place is taped off.

469
00:21:34,667 --> 00:21:36,933
It'll be hard to get in.

470
00:21:36,933 --> 00:21:39,600
We should ask around first.

471
00:21:45,367 --> 00:21:48,067
Excuse me, boss.
Can we ask you something?

472
00:21:48,067 --> 00:21:50,867
What's going on here, boss?
Why is it taped off?

473
00:21:50,867 --> 00:21:52,500
There was a bust last night.

474
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:55,767
The NCIA showed up
and caught a syndicate leader.

475
00:21:55,767 --> 00:21:58,233
Wait, what about
the vehicles up there?

476
00:21:58,233 --> 00:22:00,033
- On the rooftop?
- Yeah.

477
00:22:00,033 --> 00:22:01,933
They're gone.
They towed them all.

478
00:22:01,933 --> 00:22:04,000
Every vehicle on the roof
was towed.

479
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:05,967
The NCIA is investigating.

480
00:22:05,967 --> 00:22:07,500
We're in trouble.

481
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:12,800
Uh, boss... Where would the NCIA
take the bikes they seized?

482
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:15,367
To the NCIA impound lot.

483
00:22:16,767 --> 00:22:19,167
- All right. Thanks, boss.
- Thank you.

484
00:22:19,167 --> 00:22:21,567
- Thanks.
- We'll be on our way now.

485
00:22:21,567 --> 00:22:27,300
Gabo, that means... the NCIA
caught Tiger, not the cops.

486
00:22:27,300 --> 00:22:29,500
Those guys are big time.

487
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:31,900
Which means Tiger is
no small-time criminal.

488
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:35,100
Does anyone know
where the NCIA impound is?

489
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:37,567
Yeah, I know. It's in Deparo.

490
00:22:37,567 --> 00:22:39,333
Just a quick jeepney ride
from here.

491
00:22:39,333 --> 00:22:42,433
[ROCK MUSIC PLAYING]

492
00:22:42,433 --> 00:22:45,567
We need to get that bike back.
Let's go.

493
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:51,400
- Pa.
- Yes?

494
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:54,100
We totally fooled
that idiot Gabo.

495
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:57,933
Can you believe it? We made him
believe I didn't kill his dad.

496
00:22:57,933 --> 00:22:59,933
[BOTH LAUGHING]

497
00:22:59,933 --> 00:23:04,200
Django, let him chase
the others...

498
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:08,300
He won't even realize
we're closing in on him.

499
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:12,833
And let him focus
all his anger on the cops.

500
00:23:12,833 --> 00:23:18,067
Do you think you fooled him,
or are you the one being played?

501
00:23:18,067 --> 00:23:24,200
I know Gabo.
He's cocky and tough,

502
00:23:25,633 --> 00:23:27,200
but he's gullible.

503
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:28,600
[BOTH LAUGHING]

504
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:30,133
He believes anything.

505
00:23:30,133 --> 00:23:33,967
Django, this fight isn't just
about physical strength.

506
00:23:33,967 --> 00:23:38,400
You have to outsmart him.

507
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:42,667
Let him think
you're not his enemy.

508
00:23:42,667 --> 00:23:47,367
When he lets his guard down,
that's when you strike. Got it?

509
00:23:47,367 --> 00:23:48,533
[LAUGHS]

510
00:23:48,533 --> 00:23:49,867
I'll remember that, Pa.

511
00:23:49,867 --> 00:23:51,600
[LAUGHS]

512
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:54,167
Wait a second. Where's Ibyang?

513
00:23:54,167 --> 00:23:56,900
She's over there. I saw her.

514
00:23:56,933 --> 00:23:59,367
Okay. Hold on.

515
00:23:59,367 --> 00:24:00,967
[GRUNTS]

516
00:24:00,967 --> 00:24:05,233
Hey, go call the new guys,
quick.

517
00:24:05,233 --> 00:24:06,633
Yes, boss.

518
00:24:06,633 --> 00:24:12,033
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

519
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:13,733
[ENGINE REVVING]

520
00:24:13,733 --> 00:24:17,033
- [ROCK MUSIC PLAYING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

521
00:24:17,033 --> 00:24:19,033
[GABO] Pull over, please!
This is my stop.

522
00:24:19,033 --> 00:24:25,933
[ROCK MUSIC CONTINUES]

523
00:24:31,833 --> 00:24:33,567
[CHAINS RATTLING,
PADLOCK CLICKS]

524
00:24:33,567 --> 00:24:35,733
Looks risky.
There are guards everywhere.

525
00:24:37,833 --> 00:24:40,333
It's going to be hard
to get your bike back, Gabo.

526
00:24:40,333 --> 00:24:42,167
What's the plan, Gabo?

527
00:24:44,100 --> 00:24:46,100
We can't just walk in
through there.

528
00:24:49,767 --> 00:24:51,300
We'll go through the back.

529
00:24:51,300 --> 00:24:58,200
[ROCK MUSIC CONTINUES]

530
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:15,433
- Tekla, hurry!
- Let's go!

531
00:25:17,767 --> 00:25:19,500
[GABO GRUNTS]

532
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:24,433
- So? Is it clear?
Yeah, we're good. Let's go!

533
00:25:24,433 --> 00:25:25,900
- Let's go!
- Move, move.

534
00:25:28,733 --> 00:25:30,033
[TEKLA GRUNTS]

535
00:25:31,167 --> 00:25:34,033
Gabo, won't we get caught?

536
00:25:34,033 --> 00:25:36,033
We definitely will
if we aren't careful.

537
00:25:36,067 --> 00:25:38,000
We just need to find
Gabo's bike.

538
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:41,833
But how do we find it here?
Look at all these cars.

539
00:25:41,833 --> 00:25:48,733
[ROCK MUSIC CONTINUES]

540
00:25:54,333 --> 00:25:55,767
Lee, Lao.

541
00:25:55,900 --> 00:25:57,900
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

542
00:25:58,033 --> 00:26:00,267
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

543
00:26:00,567 --> 00:26:02,133
Listen up.

544
00:26:02,867 --> 00:26:04,233
None of you noticed

545
00:26:04,900 --> 00:26:07,467
that we were being followed
back in Chinatown?

546
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:13,367
I wonder who crossed paths
with my brother.

547
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:16,367
[LAO] You know, Boss,
with that big of a crowd,

548
00:26:16,933 --> 00:26:18,900
it's just impossible to know.

549
00:26:19,033 --> 00:26:20,500
[LEE] It could be anyone.

550
00:26:20,933 --> 00:26:23,400
But until we figure out
who it was,

551
00:26:23,533 --> 00:26:24,967
we'll be fighting blind.

552
00:26:25,100 --> 00:26:27,067
Arturo will handle finding him.

553
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:28,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

554
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:30,300
But you two?

555
00:26:32,833 --> 00:26:34,767
You have a different assignment.

556
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:38,900
Find the woman
who kidnapped Victor.

557
00:26:39,033 --> 00:26:40,667
Consider it done, boss.

558
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:42,767
What's your plan for her?

559
00:26:44,033 --> 00:26:45,500
She'll pay...

560
00:26:46,733 --> 00:26:48,900
for what she did to my brother.

561
00:26:51,933 --> 00:26:57,433
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

562
00:26:57,567 --> 00:26:58,500
[SAM] You again?!

563
00:26:58,633 --> 00:27:00,100
<i> Don't forget. You violated me!</i>

564
00:27:00,233 --> 00:27:02,300
<i>- It was you who violated me!
- Scumbag!</i>

565
00:27:02,433 --> 00:27:03,600
Want me to kiss you again, huh?

566
00:27:03,733 --> 00:27:04,633
<i>- You b****rd!
- [BLOW LANDS]</i>

567
00:27:04,767 --> 00:27:06,133
<i>- Hell yeah!
- Seb!</i>

568
00:27:06,267 --> 00:27:07,200
<i> This is the NCIA!</i>

569
00:27:07,333 --> 00:27:08,633
Victor Zafra, hands in the air!

570
00:27:08,767 --> 00:27:09,933
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [CROWD SCREAMING]

571
00:27:10,733 --> 00:27:12,600
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

572
00:27:12,733 --> 00:27:13,800
[VICTOR] You guys are arrogant.

573
00:27:13,933 --> 00:27:15,000
<i> You just got lucky.</i>

574
00:27:15,133 --> 00:27:16,833
<i>It's all because of the guy
who was chasing me.</i>

575
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,467
[DELGADO]<i> Who was the man
</i> he was talking about?

576
00:27:18,600 --> 00:27:19,833
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

577
00:27:19,967 --> 00:27:20,933
[VICTOR] You can't catch me!

578
00:27:21,067 --> 00:27:23,333
[GABO] Ahh! Ahh!

579
00:27:23,467 --> 00:27:25,467
[VICTOR]<i> One of your men wasn't
</i> even the one who tackled me.

580
00:27:25,600 --> 00:27:26,967
[SAM] Tell us who that man is.

581
00:27:27,100 --> 00:27:28,367
<i>What does he have to do
with your group?</i>

582
00:27:28,500 --> 00:27:30,367
<i>Why don't you investigate him
yourself? You're good, right?</i>

583
00:27:30,500 --> 00:27:36,033
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

584
00:27:36,167 --> 00:27:37,167
[SLAMS TABLE]

585
00:27:38,067 --> 00:27:39,033
Argh!

586
00:27:39,167 --> 00:27:41,433
I really need to find that man.

587
00:27:41,933 --> 00:27:42,900
Which man?

588
00:27:43,033 --> 00:27:44,567
The one who messed up
our operation.

589
00:27:44,700 --> 00:27:45,867
The one who disrespected me.

590
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:48,100
Why would you want
to look for him?

591
00:27:49,667 --> 00:27:52,400
Because Tiger won't talk.

592
00:27:52,767 --> 00:27:54,333
I believe that guy is the key

593
00:27:54,467 --> 00:27:56,800
for us to solve
this gold smuggling case.

594
00:27:56,933 --> 00:27:58,933
Hold on, ma'am.
What made you think so?

595
00:27:59,067 --> 00:28:00,333
- What's his connection?
- Exactly.

596
00:28:00,467 --> 00:28:01,800
That's what I want to find out.

597
00:28:01,933 --> 00:28:03,800
How he's tied to Tiger.

598
00:28:04,433 --> 00:28:07,100
Is he a business rival?

599
00:28:07,233 --> 00:28:08,633
A former ally turned enemy?

600
00:28:08,767 --> 00:28:10,800
That man could lead us straight
into the full scope

601
00:28:10,933 --> 00:28:12,033
of Tiger's operation.

602
00:28:12,167 --> 00:28:15,300
He might even reveal
who else is linked

603
00:28:15,433 --> 00:28:17,733
to all of Tiger's dealings.

604
00:28:17,733 --> 00:28:18,733
But wait.

605
00:28:19,233 --> 00:28:20,900
How are we gonna start
tracking that guy?

606
00:28:21,033 --> 00:28:23,200
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

607
00:28:23,367 --> 00:28:24,867
[GABO]
<i> Let's search the whole place.</i>

608
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:26,767
I need to get
the motorcycle back.

609
00:28:27,233 --> 00:28:28,133
Come on!

610
00:28:28,267 --> 00:28:32,267
[THUDDING]

611
00:28:32,900 --> 00:28:35,067
[HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

612
00:28:39,500 --> 00:28:40,433
[INHALES DEEPLY]

613
00:28:40,567 --> 00:28:42,433
Wait a minute.
The motorcycle.

614
00:28:42,567 --> 00:28:44,067
Did we confiscate it?

615
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:46,833
Yes. It was part
of the evidence we recovered.

616
00:28:46,967 --> 00:28:52,800
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

617
00:28:52,933 --> 00:28:54,233
[SAM] Okay. Reyes, Borromeo.

618
00:28:54,367 --> 00:28:56,967
Get every piece of information
linked to that motorcycle.

619
00:28:57,133 --> 00:29:00,267
It will lead the way
for me to find him.

620
00:29:00,600 --> 00:29:01,767
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

621
00:29:06,533 --> 00:29:09,100
[TEKLA] What now, Gabo?
Too many vehicles around here.

622
00:29:09,233 --> 00:29:11,600
You all know the motorcycle
Papa was working on.

623
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:13,400
Look carefully.

624
00:29:13,533 --> 00:29:14,567
You can count on us, Gabo.

625
00:29:14,700 --> 00:29:15,767
Let's split up.

626
00:29:15,900 --> 00:29:17,500
Tekla, you'll come with me.

627
00:29:18,033 --> 00:29:18,900
Let's go.

628
00:29:19,033 --> 00:29:21,067
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

629
00:29:21,167 --> 00:29:23,933
<i>I'm looking for an
investment opportunity.</i>

630
00:29:24,067 --> 00:29:24,967
<i> Ginintuang Lupa sounds good.</i>

631
00:29:25,100 --> 00:29:27,467
<i> General Ricardo Jacinto!</i>

632
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:30,633
<i>Are you done with the people
from Ginintuang Lupa,</i>

633
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:32,367
<i> or just cooling off?</i>

634
00:29:32,500 --> 00:29:34,867
<i>Think you're strong?
Come on, let's settle this!</i>

635
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:37,467
<i>That reporter is a real thorn
in the side.</i>

636
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:38,533
<i> You know what to do.</i>

637
00:29:38,667 --> 00:29:41,000
<i>We're going to silence
Salvador's mouth.</i>

638
00:29:41,133 --> 00:29:42,667
<i> That car suits me just fine!</i>

639
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:44,300
<i>How will you even fit
with that belly?</i>

640
00:29:44,433 --> 00:29:45,667
<i>- Shush, shush!
- Hold me back!</i>

641
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:46,867
<i> Use your beauty and charm.</i>

642
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:48,167
There's a brand-new motorcycle.

643
00:29:48,300 --> 00:29:49,567
<i> We'll give it to you for free.</i>

644
00:29:49,700 --> 00:29:52,767
<i>Once we find the motorcycle,
we'll take this baby home.</i>

645
00:29:52,900 --> 00:29:54,400
- [DOGS BARK]
<i> - Run!</i>

646
00:29:54,533 --> 00:29:56,767
[DOGS BARKING]

647
00:29:56,900 --> 00:29:58,067
<i> What will you do to me?</i>

648
00:29:58,200 --> 00:29:59,467
<i> Gabo, help!</i>

649
00:29:59,600 --> 00:30:02,867
- [BLOWS, KICK LANDING]
- [MEN GRUNTING]

650
00:30:03,033 --> 00:30:03,933
[BODY THUDS]

651
00:30:04,067 --> 00:30:06,000
- [KICKS LANDING]
- [GROANING]

652
00:30:07,467 --> 00:30:09,600
<i>Get out of here!
I'll draw their attention!</i>

653
00:30:09,733 --> 00:30:10,633
<i> Gabo!</i>

654
00:30:10,767 --> 00:30:12,033
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [WATER SPLASHES]

655
00:30:12,167 --> 00:30:13,500
<i> Aah!</i>

656
00:30:14,167 --> 00:30:15,300
[METAL GATE CLANGING]

657
00:30:15,433 --> 00:30:16,600
[ENGINE ROARING]
